---
/*
 * Sector 00 — the title card.
 *
 * "Memory loaded", not "media detected": the boot sequence already detects the
 * card, reads its contacts and mounts it, so a title card announcing detection
 * AFTER all that runs the story backwards. The header says "media mounted" for
 * the same reason, and the log's first line reads MEDIA MOUNTED rather than
 * repeating MEDIA DETECTED. (Upstream #44.)
 *
 * Identity, not a fraction: `sector 00`, never `sector 00 / 11`. Against the
 * title card's "12 sectors" a fraction scans as an off-by-one bug — the map
 * carries position, the title card carries the count.
 *
 * This is the only sector with no plates, and the only out-of-fiction surface
 * in the piece (the colophon). Both live here because nothing may come after
 * the scroll track. (Upstream #36.)
 */
---

<section
    class="tc-sector"
    id="tc-sector-00"
    aria-label="Sector 00: Memory loaded"
>
    <p class="sector-head t-eyebrow">
        <span>sector 00</span>
        <span class="rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>media mounted</span>
    </p>

    <h1 class="sector-title t-display" data-scramble>Memory loaded</h1>

    <p class="sector-note t-body">PKT-1987-113 · 12 sectors · head at 00</p>

    <div class="credits">
        <div class="asciimark" id="tc-asciimark">
            <canvas id="tc-asciimark-canvas" role="img" aria-label="Sector Read"
            ></canvas>
        </div>
        <p>
            A recovery machine reads a memory card that never arrived. Imagery:
            NASA Image and Video Library, public domain. Type: Archivo ·
            JetBrains Mono. A piece by hendri.design · 2026.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>
